ficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00868f73-2a29-5bc5-b5fa-287f2fcfd175" :question/math-academy-id "q-82304" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef3933fc56e981bd0ef6e88754c46f5ab00b15230cce5fc2ea224ecf7c1f8f0e.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2\\sqrt[3]{x}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- The function is an injection\n- The function is a surjection\n- The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/f0/f020379f306770bd87fc499ac1fef238dc6aa639fb36d5229502fcd7dd455610.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement II is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ will cover the entire interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is true because the function is both surjective and injective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e829b3-51c9-553b-9a85-45a365a040d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472772} {:answer/id #uuid "25d4d0b8-e87c-5870-9268-7bd36f45c2be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e829b3-51c9-553b-9a85-45a365a040d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472772} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab2f2b46-2c6e-5eb1-85c3-ad99eab4b5bb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b76c9ff3-fe58-5372-b648-22e1105f9edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472774} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0aa8d4-59ff-53f5-b71d-5399b2d3aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc0aa8d4-59ff-53f5-b71d-5399b2d3aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472775} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3d2d3d-6e53-548d-8c99-3c996253ee94" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7d6de4-ec23-5a7c-93c0-50dd18473fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472776} {:answer/id #uuid "2f38aaba-83e0-5b28-9931-c911d3ca9a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7d6de4-ec23-5a7c-93c0-50dd18473fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472776} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e1483-33f9-5dc2-81fd-fee7d86b3dcf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f4dc780-0892-5640-8a66-1c76dbdf69ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-170667" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n- **I.** $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$\n- **II.** $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=2x$\n- **III.** $h:Z\\to Z$ defined by $h(x)=2x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- I is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This means that \n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, for example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=4.$\n\n- II is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ 2x & =y \\\\ x & =\\frac{y}{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that\n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\frac{y}{2})=2(\\frac{y}{2})=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- III is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Notice that if $x$ is an integer number, then $h(x)=2x$ is an even number. This means that the range of $h$ is the set of even numbers.\nSo, for example, there is no value $x\\in Z$ such that $h(x)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ba97c8-22ce-5f2e-a361-5e8cdc04dd4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472484} {:answer/id #uuid "b27c6df3-9636-5cec-a7c6-7e29c522a025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b27c6df3-9636-5cec-a7c6-7e29c522a025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472485} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb62bcbf-8eae-5cf3-b5ae-4a506ba9980e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa5400a8-4d69-5498-bb26-cf35113f0a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472486} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a7df63-ed8d-5f4d-8c4c-c2ea8c9ec5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3a7df63-ed8d-5f4d-8c4c-c2ea8c9ec5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472487} :answer-field/id #uuid "08bfc292-3bc3-54f3-9448-43fbcbae4c11" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc48bae5-5a50-5365-8135-13ed7b0935d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472488} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d6054e-cf6e-54d1-a1b7-c5a2fedc0e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8d6054e-cf6e-54d1-a1b7-c5a2fedc0e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472489} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b1b7116-3a54-5f89-a498-e625b68c4215" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80ecff06-aa66-5d3f-b38e-164bc959ec2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105321" :question/problem "![](images/63/63032bf65ec10d55f9a0b968a7179db934ad6f17b869d50999e4a0f710be9977.png)\n\nFor the function $f:(-1,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- The function is an injection\n- The function is a surjection\n- The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/71/71bd13b2dd618fb60cd2e7f6c2e3807f3449e233ccb9b60e1cbd14cc928345b3.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is true because the function is both surjective and injective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e823525c-d068-59c5-b79c-15a3ccf71c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473362} {:answer/id #uuid "891e6926-8a5d-5e45-a792-62f1489010a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891e6926-8a5d-5e45-a792-62f1489010a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473363} :answer-field/id #uuid "19b384f0-5c30-5d34-9679-cd7e07ed517c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0389deac-290e-5e2b-a79a-47bb5723e7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473364} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a48bf-eee6-5f4b-abad-5b2daa66506b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0389deac-290e-5e2b-a79a-47bb5723e7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473364} :answer-field/id #uuid "410ca3ae-a20d-51b7-85fe-4743d9e9e5fd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d7f5c0-1fd8-56a4-9076-f3007ffc482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473366} {:answer/id #uuid "25dd17ba-ad09-5a8f-ab00-e55bf3b14ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d7f5c0-1fd8-56a4-9076-f3007ffc482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473366} :answer-field/id #uuid "c95d975f-eefe-5a67-a299-22eea80c5b71" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f181e810-d779-5077-8c9b-e3a1b446edcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-77480" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n- **I.** $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x+1$\n- **II.** $g:Q\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$\n- **III.** $h:Z\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)={2}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- I is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =y \\\\ x+1 & =y \\\\ x & =y-1\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that, \n\n$$\nf(x)=f(y-1)=(y-1)+1=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+1 & ={x}_{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is both surjective and injective, $f$ is bijective.    \n\n- II is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. As a counterexample, choose $y=2.$ Then there is no rational number $x$  such that $g(x)=2.$ The only numbers $x$ that satisfies ${x}^{2}=2$ are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$\n\n- III is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. As a counterexample, choose $y=0.$ Then there is no integer $x$  such that $g(x)=0,$  because ${2}^{x}>0$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac4098b-5192-54c8-8f6d-e195dab81971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473440} {:answer/id #uuid "41e127f3-fa89-57cb-ad00-c33a0ad41569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e127f3-fa89-57cb-ad00-c33a0ad41569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473441} :answer-field/id #uuid "2de55556-81c5-5e7d-8e52-b17b07e64f9e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d987b394-ce7e-50ee-bd9e-15b2865507e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473442} {:answer/id #uuid "b94f447a-92fa-59ce-915e-6bc43de8b1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d987b394-ce7e-50ee-bd9e-15b2865507e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473442} :answer-field/id #uuid "18762654-245a-5a4b-9f7e-5b1cdc56bc3f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "594452de-a12a-52ba-853d-a92da8d4b8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473444} {:answer/id #uuid "af604334-e529-5439-bf59-b34bae36264b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "594452de-a12a-52ba-853d-a92da8d4b8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473444} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b84854-48a5-5f9e-bc3e-762fc29560f5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f636c031-3e1e-5fb8-bd29-acadcf4da72e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82572" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce68b2f27b88bd43d6eebfa5380a22c00e15e4194e0ad45e6778f761667a3ceb.png)\n\nFor the function $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=x-2$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- The function is an injection\n- The function is a surjection\n- The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/2f/2ff4c0183b91aa23d780f665aa0f038b374583e9f24e245951c4c69ea5f2e5b8.png)\n\n           \n\n- Statement II is false. There is no value $x$ for which $f(x)=-2\\in R.$\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff3ba28-38e8-51bc-a126-2eff2903bff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472574} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8239a8-397c-5bf4-8f09-ac6412a0e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8239a8-397c-5bf4-8f09-ac6412a0e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d4328ce-d94c-50ad-9bc6-66e180d0c379" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de4aeae3-2eea-55f8-9d3b-f6f28669d75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472576} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb9487c-635d-5949-9980-a665c9ff96ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb9487c-635d-5949-9980-a665c9ff96ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b67704-7d9c-5f26-8cd4-1364e0247ba7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "428e1b82-e6da-5eab-9b6a-0c2af131b494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} {:answer/id #uuid "d54291b6-7ef2-55e0-96fb-76e1195bcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "428e1b82-e6da-5eab-9b6a-0c2af131b494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa69a530-25df-51d2-8915-d0fef8fbe9e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8076c0f-174e-5d1d-bedf-553b0bcc1d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-127969" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nI. $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$\n\nII. $P∧¬Q$\n\nIII. $¬P∧¬Q$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q∧(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$ and $P∧¬Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9114a1-aa7f-5df3-814e-651d0530d5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473326} {:answer/id #uuid "032cba6f-622b-5534-9122-a6d2e0064c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9114a1-aa7f-5df3-814e-651d0530d5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473326} :answer-field/id #uuid "86c73323-d68f-52e7-bb08-f5a7c5c876ad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ef3ca8-ce71-5b0e-9160-127af09d7f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473328} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7e1916-223f-548d-9df4-0fcfee646ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20ef3ca8-ce71-5b0e-9160-127af09d7f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473328} :answer-field/id #uuid "55a5184c-a43a-5418-856c-b2919b5f0f7f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b23bec9-7f3a-5e08-adee-f648ba08bc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473330} {:answer/id #uuid "c58c188c-bab8-504b-94fd-1ab2f97a5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c58c188c-bab8-504b-94fd-1ab2f97a5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473331} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c1a60f6-a246-55e5-8725-fa3150b13681" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ddf6872-c9fc-59bb-a8a4-f3c287d11e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75724" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$\n- **II.** $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5.$\n- **III.** If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$ then $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-3.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-1$ (but not $1$).\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-4{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=-4v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-4$ (but not $5$).\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(2v)=2Av=2(-3v)=-3(2v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(2v)=-3(2v),$ and $2v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $2v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-3.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eac6d8-a430-574b-a73a-7693bdbf9561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472886} {:answer/id #uuid "e86bb8e8-1da8-5c04-a45b-a4be5b0a9e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81eac6d8-a430-574b-a73a-7693bdbf9561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472886} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8bc59ab-a020-5283-b995-4b3f01b96792" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5871897b-5bfc-587f-a860-d3f937f45f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472888} {:answer/id #uuid "3d525756-0d92-5c9f-ad36-67c13bf7e9ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5871897b-5bfc-587f-a860-d3f937f45f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472888} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0415415-2a3d-5687-a51f-4a9cd8a2ce8f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112fcfe9-f163-5402-bb4c-1c126bca51d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472890} {:answer/id #uuid "448edde1-a526-52c0-ba25-3145d1c46f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "448edde1-a526-52c0-ba25-3145d1c46f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472891} :answer-field/id #uuid "db9f241c-836d-5fde-9168-5d59cd8ab428" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2006d399-9a69-519f-8bb4-45f612aefe6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213141" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={{0},{0,1}}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,X⊃Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${0}\\,R\\,{0,1}$\n- **II.** ${0,1}\\,R\\,{0,1}$\n- **III.** ${0}\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,{0}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊂{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X\\,R\\,Y$ if and only if $X⊃Y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $⊃$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $⊅$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $⊃,$ we have ${0}⊃{0,1}.$ This is equivalent to ${0,1}⊂{0},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $⊃,$ we have ${0,1}⊃{0,1}.$ This is equivalent to ${0,1}⊂{0,1},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $⊅,$ we have ${0}⊅{0}.$ This is equivalent to ${0}⊄{0},$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f77177ee-74b0-5681-92a8-ed6994ab9f9c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of Standard Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "858d1b5f-5918-5ac9-99e7-cf79a2a46733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472868} {:answer/id #uuid "2533356f-13ee-5d42-ad0e-d1a267e0303d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "858d1b5f-5918-5ac9-99e7-cf79a2a46733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472868} :answer-field/id #uuid "89cfb84f-7bdd-58d3-bfb5-bb04de54defe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e26b1ad-a11f-58c2-b68b-eb2904daa308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472870} {:answer/id #uuid "904056bb-a15e-552e-9d05-d3e6998208bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "904056bb-a15e-552e-9d05-d3e6998208bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472871} :answer-field/id #uuid "876dfd72-f2f4-50c0-a2d6-2e6b60c3e021" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "989df4ea-589f-56da-b83c-762f6d608713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472872} {:answer/id #uuid "7477b5ed-7893-5893-8195-ef07b8905aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989df4ea-589f-56da-b83c-762f6d608713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472872} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a92b2f8-77ee-5489-93de-bf8f95ddbcef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb1a702e-c18f-5fe7-b6f2-5f1506bc9396" :question/math-academy-id "q-213003" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={{0},{1,0}}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following ordered pairs is an element of the relation \"is **not** a subset of\" on $A?$ \n- **I.** $({0},{1,0})$\n- **II.** $({1,0},{0})$\n- **III.** $({1,0},{1,0})$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x⊈y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our ordered pairs in turn.\n\n- The ordered pair $({0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{0})$ is an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊈{0}.\\,✓$\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250ba09f-57fe-5dd0-975a-d2b468a0d1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472646} {:answer/id #uuid "9c891df1-6527-5ede-8429-6d73ccfed568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c891df1-6527-5ede-8429-6d73ccfed568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472647} :answer-field/id #uuid "33c474fb-e664-5c6e-88e5-5aef1be1bdc3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d6894e-adb9-5532-9b30-0021133ed0a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472648} {:answer/id #uuid "46a5c76e-74d2-57eb-8b00-086ad0c9ae19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3d6894e-adb9-5532-9b30-0021133ed0a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472648} :answer-field/id #uuid "729331d4-d482-50dd-a51c-36a8b957618a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9ace851-fe1b-5fcf-b1c4-fef78345c272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472650} {:answer/id #uuid "937b6b94-240a-5a91-be0e-92a51f8282e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9ace851-fe1b-5fcf-b1c4-fef78345c272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472650} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf12dfe2-08ac-5fa5-be0e-8055df6e4c3f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29a87319-221e-52be-a49a-7a7f42765bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130357" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of students who got an $A$ on a math exam in a class of $25$ students\n- **II.** The number of cards drawn until a red card is obtained\n- **III.** The number of books published by a publishing house in a month\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of students who got an $A$ on a math exam can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $25$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. Although drawing a red card can be interpreted as a \"success,\" there is not a fixed number of trials in this experiment.\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of books published cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822df2ab-5c24-5f38-9413-37f5aa1c2991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473464} {:answer/id #uuid "d8996723-d37c-5ead-ae67-07923891567c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822df2ab-5c24-5f38-9413-37f5aa1c2991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473464} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea73a352-768b-5694-b40a-bde32057f2c1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54204ba5-69c1-596e-bf82-5cf06d89016c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473466} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2f0299-8235-5ff0-b3b9-547374fc811a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54204ba5-69c1-596e-bf82-5cf06d89016c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473466} :answer-field/id #uuid "62d0eae5-aa19-5fb9-b9ce-5de251492c2c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a20af6e7-cf45-5f7c-b07c-8bccae7503be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473468} {:answer/id #uuid "44d28dcb-0256-5a04-865b-984aeab7ba22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d28dcb-0256-5a04-865b-984aeab7ba22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473469} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd426fda-1266-52bf-9a5b-ad1aacb1c6ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46c22425-ee4e-5a56-9d8f-8f1ffa9ada86" :question/math-academy-id "q-84748" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The ages of $20$ soccer players\n- **II.** The price of a pair of pants in a department store\n- **III.** The number of wins by a basketball team in a $30$-game season if the probability of the team winning any individual game is $55%$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The ages cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The prices cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of wins in $30$ games can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $30$ independent experiments.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e3af4b-f9ce-5ba6-b0a6-1cd12c611ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473458} {:answer/id #uuid "6f111d65-5eb1-5e5e-ab6d-178cdb7b3a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f111d65-5eb1-5e5e-ab6d-178cdb7b3a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473459} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b6a24c-c00a-580c-9242-b3b1d2c15eb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "115a22bb-c84b-5724-b6ef-88afb26dba89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473460} {:answer/id #uuid "7f635d5f-9325-57a9-92db-9b9f4c6e34fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "115a22bb-c84b-5724-b6ef-88afb26dba89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473460} :answer-field/id #uuid "746cd9ee-265d-573a-9065-80f853b84b0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d180a2b3-af05-51dd-9ef5-e5b84e65a123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473462} {:answer/id #uuid "9e23af4f-381e-5626-8adf-2fd79cc635b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d180a2b3-af05-51dd-9ef5-e5b84e65a123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473462} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee0ec6b-c2ec-51a0-b05e-4cd4f10879a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dd54609-ae0c-53a9-a2a1-7823f9aa6595" :question/math-academy-id "q-84747" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of times \"head\" is obtained when a coin is tossed $10$ times\n- **II.** The number of students in a class\n- **III.** The number of tickets sold for a concert in $3$ days\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of \"heads\" in $10$ tosses can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $10$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of students in a class cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of tickets sold for a concert cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9dd05cc-1bdb-5141-b063-9c92310da718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472652} {:answer/id #uuid "94f08a3f-89c0-5762-a545-859a0f138cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94f08a3f-89c0-5762-a545-859a0f138cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472653} :answer-field/id #uuid "60b7a4a5-d299-5c0a-93b3-71d3f35b347c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd9fac83-8f9c-5590-8209-b3d493c3318e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472654} {:answer/id #uuid "e620d4f1-7625-5296-b0a1-f21ce51413f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd9fac83-8f9c-5590-8209-b3d493c3318e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472654} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c60bd00-8be9-5ef3-a107-4d31f9dcfa16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c54a1e2-357b-527c-8373-a2a29e7c08be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472656} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ad439-af82-5223-96a3-b2e1b7a0bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ad439-af82-5223-96a3-b2e1b7a0bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472657} :answer-field/id #uuid "14ef9316-2d4c-526c-baec-1f799427372f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e06f09da-f1cd-5f64-925a-f4c6e513e373" :question/math-academy-id "q-130361" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of trees in a forest of $300$ trees that have bird's nests\n- **II.** The number of vaccines administered in a country during one season\n- **III.** The number of odd numbers obtained when rolling an eight-sided die $10$ times\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of trees that have bird's nests among $300$ trees can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $300$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. Although receiving a vaccine can be interpreted as a \"success,\" there is not a fixed number of trials in this experiment.\n\n- Random variable III could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of odd numbers obtained when rolling an eight-sided die $10$ times can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $10$ independent experiments.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Steady-State Vectors of Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16370931-5fc9-5536-9fd7-45afe61a10b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472688} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab6d543-ae19-5030-b18a-58051110b60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab6d543-ae19-5030-b18a-58051110b60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472689} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4b12e7-31db-52dd-a206-759d60508923" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71dd4b86-fcee-58b2-a783-19a83e01d1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472690} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7a9115-7513-51f1-a218-6359bc259d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71dd4b86-fcee-58b2-a783-19a83e01d1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472690} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc16e75-61f9-56a2-8f15-331022147565" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3605e075-25c5-54da-bf16-7e2307304916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472692} {:answer/id #uuid "9db4a1e3-8985-5443-8d1e-4853b29ea3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3605e075-25c5-54da-bf16-7e2307304916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472692} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb71628d-05cf-5ce1-8a2b-c44a3882f058" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62944003-1237-5928-b405-2159dbe448f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-135308" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.8 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.2\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- **II.** $Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.8 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.03+0.72 \\\\ 0.07+0.18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.75 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8e2907-6f9f-5945-87a4-4b320b3c5c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472784} {:answer/id #uuid "363acb19-a7c4-58f9-889f-e407b2331d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8e2907-6f9f-5945-87a4-4b320b3c5c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472784} :answer-field/id #uuid "51607494-5a75-5d4c-92f2-cb8a34490a90" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30463986-efbd-51fd-a6e9-b681bf1c31ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472786} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0850f2-9a46-5214-af3b-d2ee5b9d05f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30463986-efbd-51fd-a6e9-b681bf1c31ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472786} :answer-field/id #uuid "576b8513-a337-57bb-a0b8-42a8d11e9c97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da457c8-29f9-53a4-9a7b-82bd8117f5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472788} {:answer/id #uuid "9252ae02-4d55-5e0b-ab06-d7222907f63c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da457c8-29f9-53a4-9a7b-82bd8117f5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472788} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8436333-b398-5406-b728-7406ac2b71f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d807e12-6960-57f6-b74d-aa3fe66f0f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-178271" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0$\n\nII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})\\}$ is orthogonal\n\nIII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})\\}$ is orthonormal\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false since\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=3\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})⊥̸Q({u}_{3})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{3})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since the set is not even orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cc783d-0e04-52b2-86df-236d896481c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473356} {:answer/id #uuid "46a9d129-ef86-55ea-a49c-ad5f819bc93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28cc783d-0e04-52b2-86df-236d896481c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473356} :answer-field/id #uuid "3759d021-c15d-5f94-bf0f-aa713cb06b19" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a3997f5-e7eb-5b23-a96c-7b63dc3096d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473358} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3abe6b-0a1b-5b0e-88aa-5350d602ba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc3abe6b-0a1b-5b0e-88aa-5350d602ba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473359} :answer-field/id #uuid "893f8dbf-f063-518c-9f05-3f90f1e69ab0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef8546b-c47c-5327-b7a1-c64d2e6e8c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473360} {:answer/id #uuid "4219ddb4-e932-5bd3-ae3b-efec94587db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ef8546b-c47c-5327-b7a1-c64d2e6e8c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473360} :answer-field/id #uuid "69938d67-9d92-50b1-a0c1-f38ae0ed687a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40dd9397-7325-5b4d-9df5-fd6f72af0a3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76978" :question/problem "Given that $7≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=5$\n- **II.** $n=6$\n- **III.** $n=7$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=7-19=-12.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $5∤(-12).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=5.$\n\n- Note that $6∣(-12)$ because $(-12)÷6=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=6.$\n\n- Note that $7∤(-12).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae15cd1-2153-5765-8851-e11f5084cb94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472460} {:answer/id #uuid "b1941e2a-6399-5867-8fd2-8397a65c3736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1941e2a-6399-5867-8fd2-8397a65c3736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472461} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd2169e-2963-565f-b2c3-acf4b032dd7d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b3e9a3-10df-59d2-9aaf-723f387bfeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472462} {:answer/id #uuid "fda30b1a-11fa-50d8-acc0-9459616edd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda30b1a-11fa-50d8-acc0-9459616edd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c7a717-d8a9-5f11-874c-25dd59863722" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473626} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3c377ae-6819-55aa-9670-acd2f63f98b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472464} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd132f0-8e79-5cac-a8ae-b44c9aeb8654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3c377ae-6819-55aa-9670-acd2f63f98b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472464} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab28e49-bde5-57c6-bbd6-efe09ce734f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e4ac9e6-575d-537d-b731-f3556414b8f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103492" :question/problem "Given that $15≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$, which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=2$\n- **II.** $n=4$\n- **III.** $n=6$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=15-7=8.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣8$ because $8÷2=4,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $4∣8$ because $8÷4=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=4.$\n\n- Note that $6∤8.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcda3a9f-e8ac-5506-9e81-4e0c7adb449f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472862} {:answer/id #uuid "d51a1602-8985-583c-a7de-3b29ff3d2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d51a1602-8985-583c-a7de-3b29ff3d2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472863} :answer-field/id #uuid "36163b9e-ff7c-575e-882b-03250c0c2242" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0b178c-927e-5ffe-bb0f-a0a4642911b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472864} {:answer/id #uuid "49892b1b-bf63-5dba-9c8c-a402779aa85a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e0b178c-927e-5ffe-bb0f-a0a4642911b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472864} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2efcf26-7033-5f97-a19a-2bd5d52b34ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d995976-59a9-586b-825a-5a32e1e3c605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472866} {:answer/id #uuid "b699bc0a-fb3a-5599-a7b0-e1da985019b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d995976-59a9-586b-825a-5a32e1e3c605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472866} :answer-field/id #uuid "244f56e9-e3b0-51b6-90fe-1f1a02b2e44a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd2ee89b-0850-5297-a810-7e54facce40b" :question/math-academy-id "q-212522" :question/problem "Given that $-7≡-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=2$\n- **II.** $n=3$\n- **III.** $n=7$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-7-(-3)=-4.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣(-4)$ because $(-4)÷2=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $3∤(-4).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $7∤(-4).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3992319-c3cb-5cd7-aacc-a323343357a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473136} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbddcbd-2bf5-5bf2-97da-7ac2cb579d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bbddcbd-2bf5-5bf2-97da-7ac2cb579d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473137} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf25248-1682-59e7-95bb-1d361adf535a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c0376ef-55b1-5b59-b083-c9871e0d3de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473138} {:answer/id #uuid "1c79da45-cd4c-5734-b84e-b0bd3128fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c79da45-cd4c-5734-b84e-b0bd3128fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473139} :answer-field/id #uuid "d551a1fd-027b-537b-97dc-dacedd3d1459" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473964} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ce1514-9241-5a99-9a0c-8b77acadae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473140} {:answer/id #uuid "99ad0e7f-4641-5c69-9b59-23ddd75d5e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ce1514-9241-5a99-9a0c-8b77acadae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473140} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecef3e14-be54-5f11-801f-ad8edf3590fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03fcc7d2-8c99-53e1-b5b5-d7a0f5cd296f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42481" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=14$, and $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=-13$\n\n- **II.** $-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-13$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=-28$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=14\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3I & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & ={3}^{3}=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=14-27=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-14+1=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=14-14=0\\ne -28\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1c0b90-23e9-5b83-a708-3ea2a44a1581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473040} {:answer/id #uuid "d96841dd-b0ce-57d2-8366-ed50689beb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1c0b90-23e9-5b83-a708-3ea2a44a1581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473040} :answer-field/id #uuid "334c6ac2-2b02-5e0f-a88a-b19789c7086c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43066d0d-a047-5a30-8822-f5d690da8c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473042} {:answer/id #uuid "12848657-20bc-5e4e-8323-c54bfc0aa80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43066d0d-a047-5a30-8822-f5d690da8c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473042} :answer-field/id #uuid "34af04fe-4273-5909-afb6-13e9d8b36c79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216b9e19-7285-56cb-8603-99b3f8d13d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473044} {:answer/id #uuid "a0db2386-3a66-5f9c-a3fd-5640d25f6a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0db2386-3a66-5f9c-a3fd-5640d25f6a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473045} :answer-field/id #uuid "381905b6-4e83-545a-8560-cb908ea74f55" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71a6807f-51a3-5e94-a65a-0087aa5dc119" :question/math-academy-id "q-330333" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)\\times {x}_{2}(t)$\n\n- **II.** $x(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n\n- **III.** $x(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=0$ and ${c}_{2}=-3,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b89ff11c-d1b7-5405-82c1-94c7d7c99ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473046} {:answer/id #uuid "c81e64dc-937e-5cab-8f29-f5b6154dc03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c81e64dc-937e-5cab-8f29-f5b6154dc03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473047} :answer-field/id #uuid "c191f663-afad-5fac-a9f2-fac3b31f3803" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9185fe4-0729-55cd-91d0-1540bf55d2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473048} {:answer/id #uuid "44919b96-98f2-5972-8f19-8568c044e939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9185fe4-0729-55cd-91d0-1540bf55d2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473048} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eb579d0-ff0e-56d8-afd8-faecf8a98e18" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "498d2ce6-8636-51d1-aabe-214949bb04ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473050} {:answer/id #uuid "4038ba31-96d0-5ea2-80fe-ff8ad8b3e1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4038ba31-96d0-5ea2-80fe-ff8ad8b3e1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473051} :answer-field/id #uuid "a207e67d-e805-59c2-970d-7203de37688e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5a0af42-71ea-5bb3-8eb8-b8b29ef8a2c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-330354" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n- **I.** $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$\n- **II.** $x(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- **III.** $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multipliers of the first and the second terms are not constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2c3ece1-9a5e-52f4-8699-73139d9a6a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473004} {:answer/id #uuid "0563223b-220c-58df-9201-b1e95a708764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0563223b-220c-58df-9201-b1e95a708764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473005} :answer-field/id #uuid "112786af-b7c6-53b8-bad3-b5ce3ac037cf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beadd3e-28d3-5177-a991-6ac6e547dcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473006} {:answer/id #uuid "05064f80-545d-5b21-ac39-0deff32cdce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2beadd3e-28d3-5177-a991-6ac6e547dcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473006} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d9f3bb-8e2c-5510-b22f-bc287c4c9d3d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae4c9241-2ba0-574d-b41a-55b7771a6440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473008} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc3c013-0913-5495-8e49-25ca6a801a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc3c013-0913-5495-8e49-25ca6a801a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473009} :answer-field/id #uuid "6116a5f6-75a3-57f5-8b9a-87c19cf2e1cc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" :question/math-academy-id "q-214450" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[4]_{7}?$\n\nI. $-3$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $18$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[4]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $4$ modulo $7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{7} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=4+7k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{4+7k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,4-2\\cdot 7,\\,4-7,\\,4,\\,4+7,\\,4+2\\cdot 7,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-10,-3,4,11,18,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $18$ belong to $[4]_{7},$ while $6$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9484721d-864f-51dd-8b2c-88dc3adc7bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473398} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdcccb2-b950-5109-ab8d-ad162ce8aac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bdcccb2-b950-5109-ab8d-ad162ce8aac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473399} :answer-field/id #uuid "424d5d29-89a4-5745-85c3-c5b14af2f13c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer