type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472885} :answer-field/id #uuid "58f7ebd0-f7ec-51b3-8e24-dffd8a1498c6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e24d1221-5380-50fb-b4e2-6e139d57675a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213100" :question/problem "|  | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined over the sets $\\{2,4,8\\}$ and $\\{3,6\\},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(4,3)$\n\nII. $(8,6)$\n\nIII. $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{m}\\}$ and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},…{b}_{n}\\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m\\times n$-matrix (or table), where the element ${r}_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n\n$$\n{r}_{ij}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,\\text{if }{a}_{i}\\,R\\,{b}_{j}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(4,3)$ does not belong to the relation since the adjacency matrix has $0$ on the intersection of the $4$-row and the $3$-column.\n\n- The pair $(8,6)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the adjacency matrix has $1$ on the intersection of the $8$-row and the $6$-column.\n\n- The pair $(2,3)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the adjacency matrix has $1$ on the intersection of the $2$-row and the $3$-column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c544f2-0094-5efb-b9d7-430a6628b03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} {:answer/id #uuid "d6421a79-149e-5798-8b1f-119bfea53fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c544f2-0094-5efb-b9d7-430a6628b03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fafc7937-f74b-546b-b87e-a22ca804ac3f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89bbf83-2e3e-5555-a6d5-981a9278f764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} {:answer/id #uuid "cea56d01-fdfe-5736-816e-b8204e960080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a89bbf83-2e3e-5555-a6d5-981a9278f764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} :answer-field/id #uuid "8372ee30-4548-5d83-9957-bf0d65799b1f" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc580dff-bc2e-5878-b7a7-f48a863b4636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473122} {:answer/id #uuid "2be2d645-5052-599b-a84f-9d2d9883a16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2be2d645-5052-599b-a84f-9d2d9883a16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d08e1cd-2808-5a00-b091-ce22e53c0263" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42005" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff7ff1b-7d10-5900-8b02-8d8762f4648a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} {:answer/id #uuid "2a735909-2afd-58c0-8065-6f9b0fda657e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ff7ff1b-7d10-5900-8b02-8d8762f4648a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09fe1a5-baa2-5973-acbf-a84cc0ff0a30" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9738a799-c696-51e8-87a0-1ab427da9e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472606} {:answer/id #uuid "af5402ff-243c-585f-b25c-a8687187c616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5402ff-243c-585f-b25c-a8687187c616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607} :answer-field/id #uuid "1021401d-9baa-5256-9d91-aea06ee1499d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b14007f-a781-5311-9863-6ad6959abeb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472608} {:answer/id #uuid "d335439c-9eef-5cb8-852d-d00750680628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d335439c-9eef-5cb8-852d-d00750680628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609} :answer-field/id #uuid "05c9c089-5c63-5c77-b946-3743f2d68ce2" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/math-academy-id "q-129230" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8919d471-0e4c-55c1-b39e-2b46a86540d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution of a Linear Diophantine Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89dc469f-47b4-520f-b21b-08b07b7451bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473572} {:answer/id #uuid "3a733154-caa1-5094-8512-f504a530a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a733154-caa1-5094-8512-f504a530a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473573} :answer-field/id #uuid "e915d522-fb10-551b-b9c0-2a6ae97f20d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0911e3bb-5ca3-57de-848c-a3ed1bdd544f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473574} {:answer/id #uuid "81c28b99-c4a4-548b-86f9-0f49da608633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0911e3bb-5ca3-57de-848c-a3ed1bdd544f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473574} :answer-field/id #uuid "d339291e-d574-5719-a6e7-3df247786608" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eaf2778-ccc5-5f50-ad03-a8e1d231aa75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473576} {:answer/id #uuid "c98e4dd0-d468-53db-9f67-aab42d9dbd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eaf2778-ccc5-5f50-ad03-a8e1d231aa75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473576} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c7cf870-d376-5c1a-8305-823d614222f7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34033db1-99ab-5af1-b893-026e522543dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-93742" :question/problem "Which of the following pairs $(x,y)$ are solutions of the Diophantine equation $2x+5y=200?$\n- **I.** $(20,32)$\n- **II.** $(10,20)$\n- **III.** $(15,35)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each pair in turn.\n\n- $(20,32)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=20$ and $y=32,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =200 \\\\ 2\\cdot 20+5\\cdot 32 & =200 \\\\ 40+160 & =200 \\\\ 200 & =200\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(10,20)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=10$ and $y=20,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =200 \\\\ 2\\cdot 10+5\\cdot 20 & =200 \\\\ 20+100 & =200 \\\\ 120 & \\ne 200\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(15,35)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=15$ and $y=35,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =200 \\\\ 2\\cdot 15+5\\cdot 35 & =200 \\\\ 30+175 & =200 \\\\ 205 & \\ne 200\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8919d471-0e4c-55c1-b39e-2b46a86540d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution of a Linear Diophantine Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "103213a4-eee1-52b8-951a-225d0087faf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473566} {:answer/id #uuid "53523f87-d23b-5797-96b7-c1b07aa73db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103213a4-eee1-52b8-951a-225d0087faf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473566} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3750945-5563-519d-8de2-c840632071cf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "251a0a61-5483-55ee-8b3e-dc994543c886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473568} {:answer/id #uuid "d4eb30b2-c71d-5651-b1cc-c3704fa4449b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4eb30b2-c71d-5651-b1cc-c3704fa4449b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473569} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf5a7f1-a50e-5d4f-9d3c-2d0898373a0e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82e4c0e8-cd70-5672-b740-df2009447e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473570} {:answer/id #uuid "3682f9ef-0cf5-548c-ab93-1b1cefc9125e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82e4c0e8-cd70-5672-b740-df2009447e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473570} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b5a744a-bddb-5e17-b027-5a36a30654a6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "689613bd-55bf-5236-b19b-6e6b928e5d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93737" :question/problem "Which of the following pairs $(x,y)$ are solutions of the Diophantine equation $5x+6y=8?$\n- **I.** $(-2,2)$\n- **II.** $(-8,8)$\n- **III.** $(4,-4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each pair in turn.\n\n- $(4,-4)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=4$ and $y=-4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+6y & =8 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 2 & =8 \\\\ -10+12 & =8 \\\\ 2 & \\ne 8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(-8,8)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=-8$ and $y=8,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+6y & =8 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-8)+6\\cdot 8 & =8 \\\\ -40+48 & =8 \\\\ 8 & =8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(4,-4)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=4$ and $y=-4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+6y & =8 \\\\ 5\\cdot 4+6\\cdot (-4) & =8 \\\\ 20-24 & =8 \\\\ -4 & \\ne 8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "607df418-165b-5d37-aae1-d49ce8e9d3e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Linear Diophantine Equation Has a Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f0a59d0-bf7d-5ecd-8e1f-e123141cfadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473584} {:answer/id #uuid "dcefcf08-62ed-52f9-b7fb-ea0b49f3fd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcefcf08-62ed-52f9-b7fb-ea0b49f3fd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473585} :answer-field/id #uuid "5269c17c-1ffd-5bfd-8c14-5ca96bbdfe3c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2bef409-f619-51e6-94e0-f6457f0a3685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473586} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa36f0-fcc2-56e8-9927-3fa62debd7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa36f0-fcc2-56e8-9927-3fa62debd7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473587} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45c1983-86b3-5cd1-a19f-3a95ed53d6e8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "987385e9-039d-54b8-b73f-7ff76f5eb1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473588} {:answer/id #uuid "1064bb59-0abd-5531-bfb2-1b04e362e4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987385e9-039d-54b8-b73f-7ff76f5eb1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473588} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e4bd4c-8a69-5bf7-9f3f-fe25de8b0cff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8955bc35-57b9-5c55-b8c0-47deb511cca7" :question/math-academy-id "q-93798" :question/problem "Which of the following Diophantine equations have solutions?\n- **I.** $15x-20y=5$\n- **II.** $11x+9y=13$\n- **III.** $-8x+2y=5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear Diophantine equation\n\n$$\nax+by=c\n$$\n\nhas a solution if and only if $d\\,|\\,c,$ where $d=\\text{gcd}(a,b).$  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each equation in turn.\n\n- Equation I has solutions. We have $a=15,$ $b=-20,$ and $c=5.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(15,-20)=5\n$$\n\nand $5\\,|\\,5,$ our equation has solutions.\n\n- Equation II has solutions. We have $a=11,$ $b=9,$ and $c=13.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(11,9)=1\n$$\n\nand $1\\,|\\,13,$ our equation has solutions.\n\n- Equation III has no solution. We have $a=-8,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(-8,2)=2\n$$\n\nand $2\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,5,$ our equation has no solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "607df418-165b-5d37-aae1-d49ce8e9d3e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Linear Diophantine Equation Has a Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8948ea4-a4b4-5b6b-ba31-32af6140c8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473578} {:answer/id #uuid "352c13c4-661f-59c9-8c17-f99a0e6e475f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352c13c4-661f-59c9-8c17-f99a0e6e475f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473579} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dea80e2-1129-59df-89da-ce3af791e109" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb17f015-9f95-5ab0-8c04-37346e89d74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473580} {:answer/id #uuid "13f1caab-461f-5b08-b5aa-ea0b9d3bc512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb17f015-9f95-5ab0-8c04-37346e89d74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473580} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b11ffee-6b60-5f11-8662-a41e822eeaee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a816a9-4050-59d1-9baf-432d339aa8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473582} {:answer/id #uuid "1131bfa8-a0b7-5a68-b32c-3a39176d00f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1131bfa8-a0b7-5a68-b32c-3a39176d00f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473583} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa8a403-8182-54e7-a594-b436fc763ccd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccf1e2c5-efff-5b3d-ba7c-30f178649720" :question/math-academy-id "q-93795" :question/problem "Which of the following Diophantine equations have solutions?\n- **I.** $3x+7y=11$\n- **II.** $-3x-9y=2$\n- **III.** $-12x+15y=21$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear Diophantine equation\n\n$$\nax+by=c\n$$\n\nhas a solution if and only if $d\\,|\\,c,$ where $d=\\text{gcd}(a,b).$  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each equation in turn.\n\n- Equation I has solutions. We have $a=3,$ $b=7,$ and $c=11.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(3,7)=1\n$$\n\nand $1\\,|\\,11,$ our equation has solutions.\n\n- Equation II has no solution. We have $a=-3,$ $b=-9,$ and $c=2.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(-3,-9)=3\n$$\n\nand $3\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,2,$ our equation has no solution.\n\n- Equation III has solutions. We have $a=-12,$ $b=15,$ and $c=21.$ Since\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(-12,15)=3\n$$\n\nand $3\\,|\\,21,$ our equation has solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "740bd403-f1e6-5a92-a2b9-efa1ee0f552f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} {:answer/id #uuid "5170cfef-7833-5d81-bf15-5bd1c2583c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740bd403-f1e6-5a92-a2b9-efa1ee0f552f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ab5fa05-0008-5864-bfbd-37a853fa3a21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13931620-6744-5279-819c-a867d3d2f624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472744} {:answer/id #uuid "89f7ef7d-3d29-5bcd-86e4-6ccb6a042395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89f7ef7d-3d29-5bcd-86e4-6ccb6a042395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745} :answer-field/id #uuid "0562aeab-6992-5c67-82d7-eee722fd8045" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194dcf31-6ded-5f7d-8ad4-8503fc14610b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} {:answer/id #uuid "cff66d04-5359-528e-90cc-f15b10b85371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "194dcf31-6ded-5f7d-8ad4-8503fc14610b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfac123-c198-5997-bc78-bc4c79e3be46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b65bfe0-6178-564e-825d-19d4ac9443d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-150012" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a3961346a4bcb0d94e46caf6d6ed1253dc56fb4761db07b11829e329bc2fa8d.png)\n\nConsider the part of parabola and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the part of parabola is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works against the particle for $x>0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x<0.$ \n\n![](images/af/af80eab6427f376084301c03715fd098cfe4a1c816dcd72d3e1129cfa35ff29d.png)\n\n \n\nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/a2/a26ca79400bf30aa891543d30a052a6e8ec071ccb48fcd8c418fe0a713dad212.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0162ba-5ef3-5ddf-8884-68e373c833a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472526} {:answer/id #uuid "10f070d6-ca76-58f9-8198-433b788e83cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10f070d6-ca76-58f9-8198-433b788e83cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472527} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22ff3ac-6762-5a5a-a846-c9c1ac079ce7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a55ad75-30aa-5338-9705-0e8bb5a17796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472528} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfb901c-eb55-5a16-8c43-2a7bc4df1694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a55ad75-30aa-5338-9705-0e8bb5a17796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472528} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e84a8a1-9e86-5904-8f0e-d9bd26a8cf86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf9bee40-6700-53ec-bc0a-8c4fbe9bdd4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472530} {:answer/id #uuid "35fcedff-2ccf-5690-9d0e-4989e5420282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf9bee40-6700-53ec-bc0a-8c4fbe9bdd4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472530} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2b2811-e1ba-5e92-bdc1-f1a06a417ca6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "277ca4a2-1c02-58e4-b62f-d0e1176e96df" :question/math-academy-id "q-125499" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8ffc97d4fc442503eb5b59e01f317cc7a77cf57d041e16807aa0645f962a5aeb.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the three-quarter circle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/c9/c9805268d9f4984983c3cc5e2200a0c22d804bc67076a3505ad35471693c037b.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/da/dafb4d468e7711a804a5141301a02331bb5c7900f018a8ecdb6fd382bc05b799.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c75fe3-0f58-55e1-8f86-a88338d5cfcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472520} {:answer/id #uuid "a60b9432-a58a-5243-9f31-007a718f9157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a60b9432-a58a-5243-9f31-007a718f9157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472521} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce59e55-a6c7-5acf-b0ee-3ead7fb9939a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1a6c81-b372-55cc-97ce-f7cde5c58ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472522} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd28fc9-2509-520a-9b6e-b710a4fcd873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1a6c81-b372-55cc-97ce-f7cde5c58ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472522} :answer-field/id #uuid "69033084-6739-5ed3-8082-9c13508586c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f261d4a8-0a18-578f-91e8-66fc2b9fc81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472524} {:answer/id #uuid "f8017c78-c722-5466-81ee-36047fd63b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f261d4a8-0a18-578f-91e8-66fc2b9fc81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472524} :answer-field/id #uuid "149a514a-7fb2-5fae-8638-fa7be7c75462" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "429525c1-21c9-588e-9357-69745fab8529" :question/math-academy-id "q-125488" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f712612e5cf628e2cf6f2aac5195bf98b620edee4cab1791829a4ade13bcee15.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/87/8726ab8c3d764016e1bfa5206769674b6809ab3ea047b03734ae5141f0b553b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/56/56e77c37324ca2f28c0a09d762d1e5e1f4a29f5f00695e5cbadca748d92b1c6f.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862b5ba7-c160-5733-9f50-a71ae76ca34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472544} {:answer/id #uuid "e41ef8d6-645f-5335-a725-5df3f79d720b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862b5ba7-c160-5733-9f50-a71ae76ca34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472544} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6758123-2b6f-5ca7-b758-0977ff127c63" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87432ad0-fee2-5a6d-93c2-e0fdd6855b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472546} {:answer/id #uuid "a81d96e7-72a4-5890-9d53-4c56d8d05129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81d96e7-72a4-5890-9d53-4c56d8d05129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472547} :answer-field/id #uuid "7218a528-433c-5908-a059-6caac226974f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e9d4872-a5a3-5eb5-a69c-5fd7c7c550ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472548} {:answer/id #uuid "90531cfb-e714-59c4-8c1c-8472694477e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90531cfb-e714-59c4-8c1c-8472694477e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472549} :answer-field/id #uuid "2459159f-cb74-5c50-a417-695621954be1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7554a362-8a42-5a06-a982-68a08488fe59" :question/math-academy-id "q-125687" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1ba55883d76b7e48148febcf6203a987575e78179c2fcde1963ab9db34a37738.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the сurve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/e7/e783fb958f01da9552ef4258adf4bed1f7b083520ad9a59082b5479dc2fc7d40.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/20/20798c6992f536d4f280243746f8599bd4589bd69e253caeed65150b8a9944b7.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f567e86-63a5-512d-b830-be97bedcf0c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Division Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92c9d5b-f959-5953-90a6-a8ecdbf1b02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472436} {:answer/id #uuid "d095dde9-8464-578b-92bf-70c871371f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92c9d5b-f959-5953-90a6-a8ecdbf1b02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472436} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8b01d97-65f0-5722-86fe-d4234d0c21d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cdb196b-3c66-57d4-a771-2f16dffdb90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472438} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b25acd-0ce3-5e8e-b537-d16fe94e9392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cdb196b-3c66-57d4-a771-2f16dffdb90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472438} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd839d3-3c71-56c5-b3bc-cbdfb0f3dfeb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23df32a4-4c9b-5ad1-a8ef-93ba58941242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472440} {:answer/id #uuid "18bc3fc6-b8ea-5101-a626-36ebabc05ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18bc3fc6-b8ea-5101-a626-36ebabc05ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472441} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ef972a-bbba-523c-82f9-fc664ae2cd7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdd37720-ffc4-552d-8b81-f3aa2f866efb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103026" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\nI. $k=8$\n\nII. $k=-12$\n\nIII. $k=-15$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=8.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=8,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(8,8)=8\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=8.$\n\n- If $k=-12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-12,8)=4\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-12.$\n\n- If $k=-15,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-15,8)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=-15.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f567e86-63a5-512d-b830-be97bedcf0c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Division Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5fee9c-8592-5941-94ba-f732ff2e2b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472430} {:answer/id #uuid "6e43f309-2046-5c4b-88b6-e63a40e10a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d5fee9c-8592-5941-94ba-f732ff2e2b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472430} :answer-field/id #uuid "08c83890-765e-5a1e-be4c-e431339df65e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82d50d77-6a1d-59f7-8987-baae4b552219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472432} {:answer/id #uuid "aa194468-2830-58df-af8c-0429fcc1e1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa194468-2830-58df-af8c-0429fcc1e1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472433} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebad9b6f-1dd8-5d82-a7aa-d843aa29a947" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26eda066-7454-5d62-bd57-ea93331cdf97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472434} {:answer/id #uuid "5a159447-da3a-5921-aca7-0f9c4d8484cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26eda066-7454-5d62-bd57-ea93331cdf97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472434} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5d827b-cc7e-5f2d-af32-37ff6889a8bb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eaf9f361-8af6-5a67-abf5-86a0bbac7a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103018" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\nI. $k=12$\n\nII. $k=3$\n\nIII. $k=-5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=10.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(12,10)=2\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=12.$\n\n- If $k=3,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(3,10)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=3.$\n\n- If $k=-5,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-5,10)=5\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d08864-6101-5251-8351-5c0043998d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472778} {:answer/id #uuid "1a22dbe5-0d2b-5c0a-9531-8c54bafdc81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a22dbe5-0d2b-5c0a-9531-8c54bafdc81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472779} :answer-field/id #uuid "71e4259d-b2ae-5c52-927d-7cf47899f776" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c84ccb50-f1be-591e-8bac-35014caba949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472780} {:answer/id #uuid "19621db5-93e2-50ee-9ddb-8440f2d6f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19621db5-93e2-50ee-9ddb-8440f2d6f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472781} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af95f9f-6948-54ed-b3d3-37b3b7e7a68c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b309452-f7e7-54e9-bbdf-9a3025bd85c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472782} {:answer/id #uuid "f4968354-f03a-5157-9f0d-8be8dbd50643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b309452-f7e7-54e9-bbdf-9a3025bd85c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472782} :answer-field/id #uuid "46245871-924f-5edd-8bb1-a6c28bc755b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a7fbace-2464-5d79-be05-e6f28745c3de" :question/math-academy-id "q-178014" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$\n- **II.** ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal\n- **III.** ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=12-12=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $Q({u}_{1})⊥Q({u}_{2})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{2})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})$ is not a unit vector since\n\n$$\n‖Q({u}_{1})‖=‖{u}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e50955-37f8-51bc-83cc-cb950145c252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472820} {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821} :answer-field/id #uuid "33d25ffd-2c6e-5b5b-99df-560a24530be3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1322f1f2-f4c5-54d8-87cc-355df640d02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472822} {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aeb8409-1020-570b-8cec-0822b2e40889" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} {:answer/id #uuid "78ab4291-cd70-5529-b069-e726e0430998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebe7e6e-372c-5557-a0e2-e163a4bed7dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183354" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\ge 2.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\le -2.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n- **I.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n- **II.** $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n- **III.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ or if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ if and only if $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55d9a389-0207-5627-8724-2ab06942a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472532} {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f990914-9c06-5321-9dbf-d829370622d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f7147a8-f34e-5218-b7c5-8ea2c830c0bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472534} {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5dec92-40f9-56cc-a873-06f88cbc4087" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} {:answer/id #uuid "8caa6e88-f7bc-5579-83d6-8f86c7a5803f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8664d6-4e9d-52a7-ac0d-f153ff8d27fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e8f010b-1d85-5f55-981d-5803f1cc03c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125645" :question/problem "![](images/98/981d966645eec322afbfe28a5a1f519eeab8b3557692dcce368a87fe748dddd6.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/b2/b2473eb0c505d75d2c448c1a0d714d05d42737ce8d601401e925834a25ae9e14.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/85/8513d9d15d204b6f63f310a37465d6b8dfb21239ca412bac7d3b9936f2bf5ebf.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} {:answer/id #uuid "46738186-25bf-5244-a8cd-2cfae05fe1b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} :answer-field/id #uuid "2343f5a2-9a6f-5456-bd97-3e506bdd18a6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} {:answer/id #uuid "91e139e0-9b3e-56d8-b8c4-b1714fe1291e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7751525-7c16-596e-8c69-5d8f650009fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860e69b6-35d8-5d31-ba12-9202b482813d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472542} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f14689-536e-5986-8e63-f7f4a981a39f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e87c43-f6db-5082-9277-93ef32960dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-125659" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡2y\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{1+4{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $F$ is **not** conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4x}{1+4{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071ee791-8aa1-59a9-829e-f23787b55570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473130} {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c846e82-5642-55c2-bd6c-bf9a65cc14b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} {:answer/id #uuid "2adc7349-dd06-5e86-bb35-5bbbb5b04583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} :answer-field/id #uuid "37aa9389-4822-5c22-ad9b-bf758d46df45" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2322edf-ee14-5f20-8831-ec7cadfc1dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473134} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135} :answer-field/id #uuid "873d7824-ac7f-5ce0-ad45-49263a39fd15" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **II.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04206f72-e018-5925-a58f-179e897595dc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Existence of a Multiplicative Inverse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1384975-63d7-58f2-8a6b-f8fdaada1f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472934} {:answer/id #uuid "521a10a6-eef6-5cd6-bd3f-231097c31451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521a10a6-eef6-5cd6-bd3f-231097c31451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472935} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f28d54a-dfdb-5e09-b708-b52564ee8577" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3b8825-e5b5-54ec-b721-9ad318dcc51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472936} {:answer/id #uuid "e24649a2-69bb-5929-abb1-8ddb05e612d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e24649a2-69bb-5929-abb1-8ddb05e612d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472937} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b3bf3ce-97bb-590a-b2bf-ed60251bd0f7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e79cc22-91aa-5d45-9a33-77cf7359f63c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472938} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e8996f-9c1b-5aaf-b989-181aff8b6783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e79cc22-91aa-5d45-9a33-77cf7359f63c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472938} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbfb1ebd-2d8d-5340-9f10-6ab0440a9844" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d34f2bd-1406-50c4-9338-867f1ecca34e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213405" :question/problem "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36?$\n- **I.** $5$\n- **II.** $13$\n- **III.** $24$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $5$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(5,36)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $13$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(13,36)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $24$ does *not* have a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(24,36)=12\\ne 1.\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04206f72-e018-5925-a58f-179e897595dc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Existence of a Multiplicative Inverse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c0cc1a3-a6c9-58b2-b8d1-fdb7cfba42c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472940} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e8c3d3-362b-5f70-8fb3-4119be1b3ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e8c3d3-362b-5f70-8fb3-4119be1b3ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472941} :answer-field/id #uuid "91bef76c-13bb-5852-bdd3-66c94432ec9a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1475d576-2b3a-586e-ad14-f522dc43fb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472942} {:answer/id #uuid "cab0102c-224e-5fed-955e-8e93f9a41667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab0102c-224e-5fed-955e-8e93f9a41667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e331d51-05c9-592c-a896-a426f9be52d3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65760075-59ce-55f0-8242-d07135bc4821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472944} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee14e2-3c7d-55b4-808d-d5ddf27eead3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee14e2-3c7d-55b4-808d-d5ddf27eead3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472945} :answer-field/id #uuid "3440b723-fef3-5a18-9e35-d09861f3ace7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af0eb712-6f36-542d-b37c-e07c5fedf4a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-213407" :question/problem "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27?$\n- **I.** $11$\n- **II.** $16$\n- **III.** $23$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $11$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(11,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $16$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(16,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $23$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(23,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65e9c4fd-dae7-5858-b008-ca0e144fa64a" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Binary Relations Using Digraphs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08d4af0-3773-548f-9fff-8a490f817fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472916} {:answer/id #uuid "59490e6a-5908-57a3-8fef-747cf7e201bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59490e6a-5908-57a3-8fef-747cf7e201bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472917} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f20679a-5582-56e8-8163-a7d88ca1181c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203fb9b8-f545-5d2f-89ff-f4983703dc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472918} {:answer/id #uuid "59cd232f-66c8-56d0-9097-b8c0d32be4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203fb9b8-f545-5d2f-89ff-f4983703dc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472918} :answer-field/id #uuid "91133de6-9099-5c69-a30a-e54e18188597" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa1d7eb8-65e2-508b-bd06-79c281dcc46b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472920} {:answer/id #uuid "b489d262-5a96-5a75-a605-5ac9116d6ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b489d262-5a96-5a75-a605-5ac9116d6ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472921} :answer-field/id #uuid "d300fddb-6ab1-5e91-97cd-d78d9057470d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "538c45af-5de6-56ca-85b6-7f902af26d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-213261" :question/problem "![](images/de/ded4e8a94730585809c5534fee8d401481c919d529a67cd088e96b8797f2b237.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set $\\{2,5,8\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(2,8)$\n\nIII. $(8,5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation can be visualized using a directed graph (digraph), where \n\n- the nodes (vertices) of the graph are elements of the underlying set,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines an arrow from node $x$ to node $y$,\n\n- each pair $(x,x)$ from the relation defines a loop from node $x$ to itself.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(2,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has a loop from the node $2$ to itself.\n\n- The pair $(2,8)$ does not belong to the relation since the directed graph does not have an arrow that starts at the node $2$ and ends at the node $8.$\n\n- The pair $(8,5)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has an arrow that starts at the node $8$ and ends at the node $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65e9c4fd-dae7-5858-b008-ca0e144fa64a" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Binary Relations Using Digraphs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76eb6889-3903-5edc-98cf-ffd76ae6f40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472922} {:answer/id #uuid "0324bb18-7e2f-576d-80aa-e4ccc4597d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76eb6889-3903-5edc-98cf-ffd76ae6f40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472922} :answer-field/id #uuid "109d8a94-675f-5c64-b6b6-51754537b1d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c25da07-3830-504c-bc1f-9005b4d54e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472924} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1f0bc5-8009-572b-a024-da860c0859bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c25da07-3830-504c-bc1f-9005b4d54e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472924} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1ff63a-21d1-5f38-bde1-a61924e06067" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a4af93a-29f9-5457-ba20-8e433aa33dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472926} {:answer/id #uuid "59a904d2-6dee-568a-8bc7-4dc108da32a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59a904d2-6dee-568a-8bc7-4dc108da32a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472927} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb268383-61d6-5ba6-b042-e4302740ef46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ba430a9-b9f3-5dc8-a610-c4d7d7129920" :question/math-academy-id "q-213262" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b23d63f453246fb606969ba651104097fca785324d5d0fd2203e176dda19fa5.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set $\\{\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma \\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(\\beta ,\\gamma )$\n\nII. $(\\gamma ,\\alpha )$\n\nIII. $(\\alpha ,\\beta )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation can be visualized using a directed graph (digraph), where \n\n- the nodes (vertices) of the graph are elements of the underlying set,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines an arrow from node $x$ to node $y$,\n\n- each pair $(x,x)$ from the relation defines a loop from node $x$ to itself.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair  $(\\beta ,\\gamma )$ does not belong to the relation since the directed graph does not have an arrow that starts at the node $\\beta $ and ends at the node $\\gamma .$\n\n- The pair $(\\gamma ,\\alpha )$ does not belong to the relation since the directed graph does not have an arrow that starts at the node $\\gamma $ and ends at the node $\\alpha .$\n\n- The pair $(\\alpha ,\\beta )$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has a an arrow that starts at the node $\\alpha $ and ends at the node $\\beta .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "220647d1-71b8-5d0a-b497-e5d3ad7b6da2" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Binary Relations Using Graphs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a081b648-7c74-52dc-bd21-4da83424265e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472892} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb51f4d-4bd3-568b-b3ec-51a5663d12d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eb51f4d-4bd3-568b-b3ec-51a5663d12d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472893} :answer-field/id #uuid "6af81474-42ec-5dbf-8753-90a57f84075d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7db5d13-725a-5c92-a57a-8702a6d96e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472894} {:answer/id #uuid "201ffc3d-9b6b-5e51-86fe-fd882590eb9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7db5d13-725a-5c92-a57a-8702a6d96e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472894} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaa1ac0f-c1ae-5b80-ba69-f2006afe8c18" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c8b39c-8e3b-5f88-b2b5-d91157706297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472896} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4aa1c2-d50b-5650-b4a2-854650814eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc4aa1c2-d50b-5650-b4a2-854650814eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472897} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38545ae-c736-5805-8a9e-09fed758aff1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e27df10f-2205-5c33-84a9-013636e28935" :question/math-academy-id "q-213167" :question/problem "![](images/35/35756183a7b4bf08baffb00d1f35dcc370b0e58831554daafa58d8f3d4359ab6.png)\n\nThe plot of the binary relation $S,$ defined over the set $X=\\{2,4,6\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(4,4)$\n\nIII. $(6,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(2,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(4,4)$ does not belong to the relation since the plot does not contain a point with such coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(6,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b51a22-f7bb-516c-8946-37f7bb536744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472910} {:answer/id #uuid "7e001c66-2d5e-5fc7-9dbc-75651f93ff2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b51a22-f7bb-516c-8946-37f7bb536744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472910} :answer-field/id #uuid "913db174-dca4-594b-9349-a0c1ec9bdf75" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb56dc5f-3259-5b31-bf7c-98631cb8f596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472912} {:answer/id #uuid "8007d323-54e1-5ead-962c-cf2ea1cafe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8007d323-54e1-5ead-962c-cf2ea1cafe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472913} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0f55f7c-bbee-5d76-9c4b-0e605262a0f8" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc35629f-7217-578b-9b12-67f715419ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472914} {:answer/id #uuid "729c04b6-1d28-5013-bdf4-e11e5a5716c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc35629f-7217-578b-9b12-67f715419ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472914} :answer-field/id #uuid "304f4a81-f362-5264-ba0f-bf630eeb8f19" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "653fba49-a6b9-5e57-b514-cf99f2424cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-213246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **R.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡2y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **S.** $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **T.** $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $y≡x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,1)\\notin R$ since $1≢2(1)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ while\n\n- $(7,7)\\in R$ since $7≡2(7)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≡x\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is irreflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\notin T$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≢x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5e9fa8-fe85-584f-9357-ebf63d048548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472904} {:answer/id #uuid "66b4445c-dbcb-5102-9c36-f0a58c26a8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c5e9fa8-fe85-584f-9357-ebf63d048548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472904} :answer-field/id #uuid "47d00bf4-25af-50a2-a5c7-60cf25635139" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7693ccf5-ebef-506c-9ea0-9937ffdc087d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472906} {:answer/id #uuid "701be496-842e-571f-bace-1e77be1e0583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "701be496-842e-571f-bace-1e77be1e0583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472907} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c7a48d-a097-5db1-8647-b1c560da077b" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd1fefe6-97a4-519e-b49e-cd175d9f6343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472908} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0313a3-8030-57e9-8c51-ecd36a905e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd1fefe6-97a4-519e-b49e-cd175d9f6343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472908} :answer-field/id #uuid "c942da9b-3098-5e2c-bc69-59eb0d35646e" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213240" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **R.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x+y)∣10,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **S.** $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $4∣({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **T.** $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y+1),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin R$ since $2+2=4$ and $4∤10,$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in R$ since $1+1=2$ and $2∣10.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n4∣({x}^{2}-{x}^{2})\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin T$ since $2∤(2+1),$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in T$ since $1∣(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29f9cbb-000d-5b8c-9f6c-2b45ca8f9c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472898} {:answer/id #uuid "bb936d2a-d218-5632-94f0-f74248519d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb936d2a-d218-5632-94f0-f74248519d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472899} :answer-field/id #uuid "61b2f428-c732-5a03-845e-71d541cb66c5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e88f6e62-a168-5578-bc6f-cde1ddbb2379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472900} {:answer/id #uuid "01a0001b-a449-59f4-9d85-6090aa040780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88f6e62-a168-5578-bc6f-cde1ddbb2379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472900} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cb8e60-7f3f-5cab-a5a8-f9261791e5bd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cff02f99-4992-5465-bf2c-8b903daf43f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472902} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6fc2e4-b2f4-5892-9fc2-d6d8f7bc0bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6fc2e4-b2f4-5892-9fc2-d6d8f7bc0bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472903} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3b864c-298a-50d4-be87-b47b4870ee67" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" :question/math-academy-id "q-213228" :question/problem "![](images/03/03ddf06402ad38708d232cf28783c817bf881965d54650eb158e7ffca4ea76a2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A=\\{1,2,3\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/b6/b63d99459e8271e70ec36fd417d67565f3d5e77316815d49c235468e174aa1e9.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa80fb6-08ad-5ab5-9b84-28cc06a2687a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472712} {:answer/id #uuid "e3efc5a3-366a-5a29-a48e-d8ddbd406cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3efc5a3-366a-5a29-a48e-d8ddbd406cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472713} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f52a81-37f3-5813-b236-8991da4825e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f833641-c372-57ac-ba60-2d4f8e69063b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472714} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b19d5-5886-5396-88bc-bf5f4bbca3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b19d5-5886-5396-88bc-bf5f4bbca3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472715} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28af8a5-3e58-5224-82c5-28d1a62a2d64" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2a9643-7098-501a-9ebc-7cfb1fab4258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472716} {:answer/id #uuid "60b54385-bc72-5ca7-92b5-e42793fb3038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2a9643-7098-501a-9ebc-7cfb1fab4258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472716} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1fe5d17-2a3a-5760-88f2-5077ef1873c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "062c6773-1c0f-5106-b2b7-7c444f43389f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139820" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}|{X}_{i}|$\n\nII. $min({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{13},{X}_{15})$\n\nIII. $max({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15},\\sigma )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression I is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ only.\n\n- Expression II is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population standard deviation $\\sigma .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91928ab5-1c08-5709-ade9-42c3fbbc3f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472736} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee1a951-eaaf-5f12-8f31-8f125d603255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91928ab5-1c08-5709-ade9-42c3fbbc3f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472736} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5bc247-9c01-53e3-aadd-ed34804268a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d5702a5-502e-5b8d-9267-895c288c6f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472738} {:answer/id #uuid "af515352-e650-5ec1-92cb-48d3ce1f3514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d5702a5-502e-5b8d-9267-895c288c6f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472738} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ff48ec-fbac-56c6-88aa-5530077f7640" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f929db08-b244-5145-89ee-3131d2530bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472740} {:answer/id #uuid "df817a80-9731-505c-9947-3f51347deb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df817a80-9731-505c-9947-3f51347deb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472741} :answer-field/id #uuid "b551a732-145c-5747-b844-8f4d584df8bc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4893e2e1-c5c0-525e-90bd-45f0ee89d95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143552" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n- **I.** $\\mu \\cdot \\sigma -\\text{min}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16})$\n- **II.** $\\mu -\\text{median}({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{16})$\n- **III.** $\\sigma -max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{15})$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expressions I and II are *not* statistics. They are functions that contain the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression III is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab934dba-e3a2-5d59-ae83-e95f06179b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472700} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7b43a7-81e3-5385-a0ab-8aadc7cfbe8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f7b43a7-81e3-5385-a0ab-8aadc7cfbe8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472701} :answer-field/id #uuid "d026cafa-0a30-51b7-99c1-cb46a04536a8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "063a719d-4200-54e4-9e1b-9c0087bfc4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472702} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ed26bd-c371-53d5-9888-89c529c6ff4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ed26bd-c371-53d5-9888-89c529c6ff4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472703} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d049014-59a4-5655-9e05-070f06635b97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "864619e5-82e3-5fc8-9c87-5b622c8d6d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472704} {:answer/id #uuid "b70d53e4-20bc-5813-bb56-65a2b340805a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "864619e5-82e3-5fc8-9c87-5b622c8d6d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472704} :answer-field/id #uuid "736ceb2f-5c2e-5a72-8e8c-82929b1731e1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ccfb8c1-3a4b-5435-8003-dc3e546488df" :question/math-academy-id "q-139813" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{9}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n- **I.** $max({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{9})$\n- **II.** $\\text{median}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{9})$\n- **III.** ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{9}{(\\frac{{X}_{i}-\\sigma }{\\mu })}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expressions I and II are statistics. They are functions of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{9}$ only.\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu $ and the unknown population standard deviation $\\sigma .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-